// Emit config. `tsconfig.json` is the *check* config and covers everything the
// compiler should see, including `extensions/` — the only file a consumer of
// this package actually loads (#21). This one narrows that to what we build.
//
// `extensions/` is deliberately checked but not emitted: pi loads the .ts
// source directly through jiti, resolving `typebox` and
// `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` from its own install via a runtime alias.
// Compiling it here would put a second, unreferenced copy in dist/ whose
// imports resolve differently from the one that actually runs.
//
// The `test/` include and the missing `rootDir` are inherited defects, not
// choices — dist/ currently mirrors the repo as dist/src/ + dist/test/, which
// is #80's job to fix. Kept identical here so this issue changes nothing about
// what gets built.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts"]
}
